  "question": {
    "text": "In a meter bridge, the wire of length <math><mn>1</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>m</mi></math> has a non-uniform cross-section such that, the variation <math><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>R</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>l</mi></mrow></mfrac></math> of its resistance <math><mi>R</mi></math> with length <math><mi>l</mi></math> is <math><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>R</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>l</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#8733;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><msqrt><mi>l</mi></msqrt></mrow></mfrac><mo>.</mo></math> Two equal resistances are connected as shown in the figure. The galvanometer has zero deflection when the jockey is at point <math><mi>P</mi><mo>.</mo></math> What is the length <math><mi>A</mi><mi>P</mi><mo>?</mo></math><br /><br /><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/apieykswnmsrcqqwlnylvdzinlvniybqlnsthhxartfgziarjs.png\" />",
    "image": null
  },
